# This file is what keeps a deployment's keys out of its own commits.
# The root .gitignore matches `.env` / `.env.*`,
# which does NOT match hosts/<id>/runner.env or agent.env (the grading key, the agent key
# and the model credential of a live rollout). `*.env` below does.
# secrets — never committed
.env
*.env
# campaigns (docs/campaigns.md): the artifact store is the runs bucket, the launch host
# keeps the scoring inputs, and nothing under here is ever committed — legitimacy lives in
# the status files and the manifests' histories, not in git
campaigns/*
# the live hosts' staging dirs (seeded scaffold, runner.env + agent.env, ec2.json): transient.
# launch_rollout.py --dry-run leaves one behind on purpose, keys included.
hosts/*
# one deployment's AWS ids (account, VPC, bucket, AMI): the file you create from
# host/ec2/infra.example.json. Not a secret, but it names your account, so it stays local.
host/ec2/infra.json
# flat run stores from before campaigns/ existed; still ignored in case a checkout has them
runs/
# scaffold node_modules / build outputs (scaffolds are committed WITHOUT deps)
scaffolds/*/node_modules/
scaffolds/*/.expo/
scaffolds/*/build/
scaffolds/*/ios/
scaffolds/*/android/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/tmp/
